  requestId    905b46fc56b6fa34fb908a7a0e039346
  answer       Lumail.io is an AI-native email platform that combines newsletter campaigns, automated workflows, and transactional email into one organization-scoped system [1][2]. It is designed for developers, newsletter writers, and teams who want to operate email via AI agents, code, or a visual dashboard [2][3].

Pricing is based exclusively on monthly email volume, with unlimited subscriber storage on all plans [4][2]. The free plan includes 3,000 emails per month, while paid plans start at $20/month for 40,000 emails [2][5].

Key features include an AI-assisted editor, visual workflow builders with A/B testing, and 139 MCP tools for AI-agent integration [1][2]. Unlike Mailchimp or beehiiv, Lumail does not charge based on list size or subscriber tiers, making it predictable for large, dormant lists [4][3].

Compared to Mailchimp, Lumail is a programmable email system rather than a broad multichannel marketing suite [3][6]. Compared to beehiiv, Lumail focuses on integrated transactional and lifecycle email rather than publication-specific features like ad networks or hosted website management [5][7].
